# Keep this file. It is the only tracked thing in this directory and its whole
# job is to make sure `import /etc/caddy/extra/*.caddy` in deploy/Caddyfile
# matches at least one file on every box.
#
# An import glob that matches nothing is, depending on the Caddy version,
# either a warning or a refusal to load the config. There is no reason to find
# out which on a box that terminates TLS for more than one product, so the glob
# is never allowed to come up empty.
#
# It contains no configuration, which is valid: an imported file is spliced in
# where the import sits, and splicing in nothing but comments adds nothing.
#
# REAL SITE BLOCKS GO IN SIBLING FILES, named so the order is obvious, for
# example 10-shared-edge.caddy. Everything in here except this file is
# gitignored and therefore specific to the box it is on.
#
# A block here that proxies to a container in ANOTHER compose project also
# needs caddy to be on that project's network. Copy
# docker-compose.local.yml.example to docker-compose.local.yml and add it
# there; deploy/up.sh picks that file up on its own.
#
# After editing anything in this directory, validate before you reload. From
# deploy/:
#
#   docker run --rm --env-file .env \
#     -v "$PWD/Caddyfile:/etc/caddy/Caddyfile:ro" \
#     -v "$PWD/caddy-extra:/etc/caddy/extra:ro" \
#     caddy:2-alpine caddy validate --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile --adapter caddyfile
#
# That reads the same two mounts the real container gets and touches nothing
# that is running.
